+# pipeline yaml the checker parses (the job_dirs of .buildkite/ci_config*.yaml -
+# test_areas/, hardware_tests/, intel_jobs/ - plus .buildkite/test-amd.yaml).
+# These are pre-existing gaps, captured when the check was first added so that
+# the gate could start green. The list is meant to only ever shrink.
+#
+# Rules:
+#   * Every entry needs a trailing `# <reason>` on its own line saying why the
+#     test isn't wired into a job. A bare path is rejected by the check.
+#   * Do not add a new entry to unblock a PR without a real justification.
+#   * To remove an entry: add the test to a job's `commands` (and matching
+#     `source_file_dependencies`) in a .buildkite/ pipeline yaml, then delete the
+#     line.
